      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point. I think it will only cause a DoS, or even just a performance degradation: since pid_table[id] \u003d 0, IPIs sent to this vCPU will not be virtualized via IPIv, they will instead cause APIC_WRITE vmexits (per SDM section 32.1.6.2 IPI Virtualization Using Virtual-Interrupt Posting) which will be handled by the host for IPI emulation, i.e. those IPIs will use the legacy slow path.\n\nBut still it feels safer to check for duplicate vcpu_id anyway.\n\nBTW it looks like the original KVM\u0027s `kvm_vm_ioctl_create_vcpu()` has a similar issue (it allows userspace to corrupt pid_table[id] of an existing vCPU as a side effect of trying-and-failing to create another vCPU with the same vcpu_id), and even worse: without pKVM, `vmx_vcpu_free()` doesn\u0027t clear pid_table[id], so it remains overwritten by the no longer existing vCPU\u0027s pi_desc. So, IPI delivery to the first vCPU will not work at all, and even worse: it will cause hardware to write to freed memory (since this stale pi_desc will be freed as a part of `kmem_cache_free(kvm_vcpu_cache, vcpu)` of the failed-to-create vCPU at the end of `kvm_vm_ioctl_create_vcpu()`).",
      "parentUuid": "3dfa6799_b0f83d46",
